In article <3971@rex.cs.tulane.edu> hoang@rex.cs.tulane.edu (Hoa`ng Tie^'n Du~ng) writes:

       I once had a wizard that acquired the strength of a Babarian in a
   mysterious way.  I was not paying close attention to the events that led to
   the strength increase since I only noticed when the strength was increasing
   to 18/23 or so.  I remembered quaffing a potion that gave me a peculiar
   feeling or some other meaningless message (to me at least).  Also, the
   strength seemed to increase as I gained levels.  Does the potion have
   anything to do with this?  Could it be a potion of change?

Gaining levels increases one's carrying capacity, which is a merciful
decision on the part of the dev team.  Otherwise, wizards would
collapse under the weight of their wands.  As for the strength
characteristic, you need spinach, potion of gain ability, royal jelly,
etc. to boost it.  As far as I know, gaining levels never affects your
stats. 

